      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that those arguments are flawed, but for the sake of the debate, i really need to know the specific \"science\" they lean on. if i'm going to debunk them, i can't just say they're \"flawed\"—i need to know exactly what data or specific theories they cite. like, what are the actual claims regarding things like brain size, specific allele frequencies, or certain standardized test trends they use to build their case? could u walk me through the actual points they make, even if they're wrong? it'll help me prepare more specific rebuttals.",
